---
import ServicePage from '../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import roomImg from '../assets/images/consult-room.jpg';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../data/services';
const service = serviceBySlug('womens-health')!;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Do I need an appointment?', a: 'For most things, no. Just ask at the counter. UTI consultations are walk-in. For contraception consultations, please call first so we can check a trained pharmacist is on.' },
  { q: 'Can I talk to a pharmacist in private?', a: 'Yes. We have a private consultation room, and you’re welcome to ask for it for any conversation about your health. Just ask at the counter.' },
  { q: 'Can a pharmacist prescribe contraception?', a: 'Yes. In Queensland, our trained pharmacists offer contraception consultations for eligible women aged 16 and over, and can prescribe contraception if it’s suitable. The consultation costs $35. See our <a href="/hormonal-contraceptive-pill/">contraception consultations</a> page.' },
  { q: 'Can I get emergency contraception here?', a: 'Yes. Emergency contraception is available from our pharmacists without an appointment or consultation fee. You fill in a short questionnaire, and a pharmacist checks what’s suitable. See our <a href="/emergency-contraception/">emergency contraception</a> page.' },
  { q: 'How much do consultations cost?', a: 'Advice from our pharmacists is free. Contraception consultations cost $35, and UTI consultations have a fee that isn’t covered by Medicare. Call us or ask at the counter.' },
  { q: 'Can I see a doctor here?', a: 'Yes. Help Medical is an independent general practice located inside our store. Walk-ins are welcome subject to doctor availability, and you can <a href="/help-medical/">book online</a>.' },
];
---

<ServicePage
  service={service}
  title="Women's Health Pharmacy Gold Coast | Priceline Pacific Fair"
  description="Contraception, UTI treatment, pregnancy, periods and menopause support from pharmacists at Priceline Pacific Fair, Broadbeach, in a private consultation room."
  h1="Women’s health at Pacific Fair"
  lead="Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair in Broadbeach can help with contraception, UTI treatment, emergency contraception, pregnancy supplements and vaccines, periods and menopause, with a private consultation room whenever you want one. Advice is free, most things need no appointment, and contraception consultations cost $35. When you need a doctor, Help Medical is an independent general practice located inside our store."
  faqs={faqs}
  hub={{ name: 'Vaccinations & health', href: '/vaccination-information/' }}
  primaryCta={{ label: `Call ${site.phone}`, href: site.phoneHref, event: 'cta_call' }}
  secondaryCta={{ label: 'Hours & directions', href: '/visit-us/' }}
  dateModified="2026-10-28"
>
  <h2>What contraception help can a pharmacist give?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/hormonal-contraceptive-pill/"><strong>Contraception consultations.</strong></a> In Queensland, our trained pharmacists can help eligible women aged 16 and over start, restart, change or continue their contraception, without a GP visit.</li>
    <li><a href="/emergency-contraception/"><strong>Emergency contraception.</strong></a> Available from our pharmacists without an appointment or consultation fee. Ask at the counter for a short questionnaire.</li>
    <li><strong>Longer-acting options.</strong> We can refer you to a GP at <a href="/help-medical/">Help Medical</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <Image src={roomImg} alt="The private consultation room at Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair, used for vaccinations and pharmacist consultations" widths={[480, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px" quality={72} />

  <h2>Can a pharmacist treat a UTI?</h2>
  <p>Burning or stinging when you pass urine? Our trained pharmacists can assess and, if suitable, treat uncomplicated UTIs in women aged 18 to 65. <a href="/uti-treatment/">Find out about UTI treatment</a>.</p>

  <h2>How can we help in pregnancy and when planning a family?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Advice on pre-conception and pregnancy supplements. See <a href="/vitamins-supplements/">vitamins and supplements</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/vaccination-information/">Whooping cough and flu vaccines</a>, which are recommended in pregnancy and free under the National Immunisation Program.</li>
    <li>Checking whether your medicines, including over-the-counter ones, are suitable in pregnancy and while breastfeeding.</li>
    <li>Pregnancy tests, breastfeeding supplies and baby care.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Always read the label and follow the directions for use.</p>

  <h2>What about periods and menopause?</h2>
  <p>Painful or heavy periods, premenstrual symptoms and menopause symptoms such as hot flushes and poor sleep can all affect daily life. Our pharmacists can talk through options that don’t need a prescription, and help you decide when it’s worth seeing a GP.</p>

  <h2>What else can we help with?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Thrush symptoms: ask a pharmacist, and see a GP if symptoms keep coming back or you’re pregnant.</li>
    <li><a href="/health-station/">Free blood pressure checks</a> at our Health Station.</li>
    <li><a href="/skincare-tanning/">Skincare advice</a> for hormonal breakouts, pigmentation and sensitive skin.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When should I see a GP?</h2>
  <p>See a doctor if you have unusual bleeding, pelvic pain, a breast lump, symptoms that keep coming back, or if you’re pregnant and unsure about a medicine. <a href="/help-medical/">Help Medical</a>, an independent general practice located inside our store, welcomes walk-ins subject to doctor availability. In an emergency, call 000.</p>
</ServicePage>
